WEBVTT

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:09.790
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:20.160
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.800
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:53.890
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.550
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:07.020
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:14.330
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:21.030
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:28.260
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:50.680
I’m unsure too.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.570
About being a priestess.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.090
About going into battle.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.090
Whether those are
the right things to do.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.130
You and I are completely
different in every respect.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.350
But we’re alike in just one way.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.070
Stand up, Aer.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.480
I am your pair.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.900
Everyone, hurry up
to the left flight deck!

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:16.940
— Hurry!
— All right!

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:27.310
Mamina, let’s go.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.820
Our Simoun is waiting for us.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.710
Isn’t that why we’re here?

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:44.760
<b>The Hearing</b>

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:51.440
I’ll make them pay for
taking my big sister hostage.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:58.020
If our feelings go to pieces
again, I couldn’t bear it.

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.020
Are you scared?

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.270
Not one bit.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:05.030
I’m scared.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.120
Let’s hurry.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.450
Neviril and I are alike
in one way… What is it?

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:22.350
Never mind. What matters is
that I’m Neviril’s pair from now on.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:28.140
One second is enough. Right the ship.
We’re launching the Simouns.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.640
Rubor and Caput were destroyed?

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.100
Chor Tempest will be going out.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:37.860
Did you hear that? Keep the ship
level while Chor Tempest takes off!

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.450
We’ll launch a simultaneous
counterattack. There’s no time to aim.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:42.360
Blast away!

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.420
This is…

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.290
Yes, the fuselage Amuria and I shared.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:57.710
It looks fixed.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:58.590
Let’s go.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:05.340
You’re Sibylla Aurea’s
auriga. Do your best.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.550
Right.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:33.060
Jeez, our attacks
aren’t connecting at all!

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:35.750
They can’t hit
anything from that position.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:37.960
We’re plunging in, Yun!

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.250
Look left!

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:41.210
Neviril…

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:04.450
We’ll protect the Arcus Prima.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.530
Diamond Ri Majon.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.990
The Diamond Ri Majon…

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:39.190
The Diamond Ri Majon can
neutralize the enemy bombardment.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:44.650
Right, it is one of the most difficult
defensive Ri Majons to execute.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:49.330
The helical motors on this ship
are barely functioning anymore.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:52.280
The only way is for
them to convey us…

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:56.660
Leave it to them.
I’m sure Chor Tempest can manage…

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:05.670
We’ll hold the Diamond Ri Majon and
move out of the enemy’s firing range!

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.670
Okay, gotcha!

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:50.970
The hearing will be held this
afternoon, as soon as we arrive.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:55.500
We don’t have much time to prepare.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.520
I’d like to take this time…

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.980
…to once more go over what
happened with you, Sibylla Neviril.

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:08.570
You will see your father,
Lord Harukonf, at the hearing.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:48.820
You and I are completely
different in every respect.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:51.610
But we’re alike in just one way.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.710
Stand up, Aer.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:56.660
I am your pair.

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:21.310
I wonder if Neviril’s coming back.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:25.720
But even if Neviril does come back…

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:27.610
…what difference would that make?

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:29.570
Listen, you…

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.840
Just when we finally
got back to full strength.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:38.330
Just when I thought
we could all fly together again.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:41.830
No one’s blaming
you anymore, Mamina…

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:45.170
That’s not what I meant…

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:49.380
Looks like Dominüra
ran off somewhere too…

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:51.680
Rimone, don’t you know where?

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:52.800
Don’t ask me.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:57.020
Even if Neviril does come back…

00:08:57.020 --> 00:09:00.530
…it’s not as if we can
carry on as Chor Tempest.

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:03.570
We’ll just disband
with all members present.

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:05.930
Oh, here you were.

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:07.310
We’ve been looking for you.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:13.320
Chor Tempest sibyllae, it is almost
time for the ceremony to begin.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:16.570
I’d appreciate it
if you started getting ready.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:27.170
Nothing you did brought
about the desired results?

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:33.090
It’s too early. I still believe that
Chor Tempest has vast potential.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.170
For example?

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:37.090
Neviril has returned.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:40.640
And two of the chor’s
new recruits, Rimone and Aer…

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:44.680
…possess latent talents
unlike any sibylla before.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:49.680
The sibylla in your report,
your favorite, Rimone, eh?

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:54.450
True, Harukonf-sama’s prodding
added two more sibyllae…

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:58.580
…Sibylla Mamina and
Sibylla Yun, to Chor Tempest.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:09:59.680
Yes.

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.560
But no matter how
convincing you are…

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:06.200
…everything will be
decided soon in that room.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:13.380
Now that it’s come to this, it would
be wise to switch to our next plan.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:15.060
But…

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:19.630
…it was you who allowed the highland
agents to board the Arcus Prima.

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:22.800
Dominüra, this discussion is over.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.310
Forgive me, Neviril.

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:06.620
But I only have your
best interests in mind.

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:08.640
And your own too, Father.

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:14.690
It is true Chor Tempest’s record
is nothing short of dazzling.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:19.100
But the sibyllae have
destroyed it with their own hands.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:23.610
For Tempus Spatium’s priestesses to
feud and go at each other’s throats…

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:27.990
…asserting themselves by baring
their basest instincts, is unthinkable.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:32.180
But what of our responsibility for
not recognizing the conference…

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:36.500
…a sham, allowing Plumbum
to carry out its destructive plot.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:42.000
Chor Tempest saved our precious
Arcus Prima from the enemy’s ruse.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:45.530
Had it not been for
their excellence that day…

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:48.470
…I wouldn’t be
standing here right now.

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:49.980
We…

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:54.200
No one granted permission
to speak, Sibylla Neviril.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:55.310
I do.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:57.480
Onasia…

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:04.160
Sibylla Neviril, that day at the Spring…

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.700
…I did indeed hear
Elly’s wail of anguish.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:12.870
I’m afraid…

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:49.540
Please say what you
have to say to everyone here.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:51.700
All right.

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:57.960
We are all priestesses serving
Tempus Spatium, and as sibyllae…

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:02.440
…we’ve listened to the Simouns and
drawn Ri Majons across the skies.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:07.180
And we have also killed scores of
soldiers from neighboring countries…

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.100
…attempting to invade
Simulacrum Kyuukoku.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.190
Go on.

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:19.680
What we carried out could
almost be called slaughter.

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:23.690
We met a massive fleet of aircraft
from Shoukoku, and in the battle…

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:28.950
It wasn’t a battle.
How dare a sybilla speak like that…

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:33.200
We have already lost three
of our beloved comrades.

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:38.960
As for Chor Caput, eleven of
their sibyllae have fallen in battle.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:45.080
When the highland priestesses
gave their lives in the plot…

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:47.970
…to destroy the Arcus Prima,
even more lives were lost.

00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:53.150
There was no deceit in
their devotion to their god.

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:55.020
As priestesses ourselves…

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:59.360
…what are we supposed to believe,
and how should we act?

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:01.730
We are waging war now.

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:03.320
Enough…

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.990
That’s enough, Neviril.

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:11.110
We are gathered here today…

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:14.910
…because we must sadly bid farewell
to a number of our beloved friends.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:22.920
We traveled together and fought side
by side with these comrades of ours.

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:27.790
Even for a time
of war, their departure…

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:31.080
This was our original job, wasn’t it?

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:35.930
To offer flawless
Ri Majons to Tempus Spatium…

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:39.430
We’ll return to our
normal sibylla duties.

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:41.440
But I’m not sure how I feel.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:47.110
So you really wanted to mourn
the dead? That’s pretty gloomy.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:51.100
Aer, that’s not what I meant to say…

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:57.620
This is the last Ri Majon we’ll ever do
as Chor Tempest. Keep that in mind.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:01.880
I wonder if we’re really
qualified to mourn the dead.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.630
Qualified or not, it’s duty.

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:09.080
I just want to get
this over with. That’s all.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:15.640
Sibylla Paraietta,
please begin the ceremony…

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:19.270
…to commemorate those who gave
their precious lives for their country.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:23.310
Yes, sir.
We’ll offer the Ri Majon of the Fields.

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:28.540
I am not looking to blame
anyone for this war we’re waging.

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:32.780
No matter how tragic and painful it
is now, I believe it was meant to be.

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:36.760
Whether or not that is
Tempus Spatium’s will…

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:39.610
…it makes no difference to me now.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:44.620
I no longer even care whether
it’s God’s will anymore.

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:51.760
However, I do have
one question for you all.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:57.360
Despite all this, can I still
call myself a Simoun sibylla?

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.520
Sibylla Neviril…

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:07.270
As long as you yourself wish it,
you may still consider yourself…

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:10.280
…a Simoun sibylla.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:12.610
All right.

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:26.510
Wait! You made a comment
we simply can’t overlook.

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:32.280
We can’t allow you to get away with
saying you don’t care about God’s will.

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:33.550
Please wait.

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:39.310
I have something to say to all of you.

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:45.550
You’re from Chor Rubor…

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:48.060
My name is Vura.

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:50.070
I summoned her.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.820
Guragief, how dare
you take such a liberty?

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:57.070
What is it that you
have to say? Sibylla Vura…

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:59.030
…speak now.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.030
Onasia…

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:05.080
I will.

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:11.490
Chor Tempest is the chor all Simoun
sibyllae worship and take pride in…

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:13.210
…the finest chor of all.

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:16.860
On behalf of all Simoun sibyllae…

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:20.470
…I beg you to consider
preserving Chor Tempest.

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:25.530
Do you mean
Chor Tempest as sibyllae?

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:29.980
Or Chor Tempest as
a squadron of warriors?

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:35.850
You say you want us to preserve
Chor Tempest, but which one?

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:38.140
Twelve sibyllae…

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:41.990
…who become each other’s pairs
and draw Ri Majons across the sky.

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:45.840
There is only one Chor Tempest.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:16.610
Three o’clock!

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:18.990
The enemy.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:20.530
Para-sama, look.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:21.780
I know!

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:24.620
What is it?

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:26.500
I’ve never seen anything like it.

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:33.200
Is that a new type of cannon?
But I’m sure we can…

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:37.840
Those are no cannons. They’re
headed straight for the great temple.

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:06.330
Let’s go, Rimone.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:08.620
We’ll disengage from the Ri Majon
and shoot those things down!

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:18.960
Everybody’s always ganging up
on us and making us suffer like this.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.590
I suppose we…

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:22.800
This must be our fate…

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:25.510
One way or another,
we’re bound to do Ri Majons.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:44.490
Mamina! Look!

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:49.200
How can there be so many?

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:53.210
Only the Iron Ri Majon
can destroy a fleet that size.

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:58.610
We can’t. It takes all six Simouns
to perform the Iron Ri Majon.

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.140
The Iron Ri Majon…

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:39.420
Neviril!

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:43.550
What a lovely breeze.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:46.510
Vura?

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:50.470
Welcome back, Neviril!

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:52.890
I’ve come home, everybody.

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:58.980
I have good news. They won’t
disband Chor Tempest after all!

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:00.610
Goody!

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.080
Isn’t that great, Mamina?

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:04.320
Yes, it’s wonderful!

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:06.320
Hey, what’s the matter?

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:12.080
I’m so happy. This means we can fly
our Simouns across the skies again.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:16.730
I’m so glad, Para-sama.
We’ll be flying together again, right?

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:19.280
What in the world
happened down there?

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:24.800
Something must’ve
happened, right? Neviril, Vura!

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:36.980
Now that Chor Tempest
won’t be disbanded…

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.690
…we must repair
the Arcus Prima at once.

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:43.760
I wanted you to move on to
the next phase of your life.

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:49.700
I can’t lose face in the high council.
Chor Tempest can’t go on as it has.

00:21:57.420 --> 00:22:01.960
Until the repairs on
the Arcus Prima are completed…

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:07.970
…we’ll board the Messis and be
charged with border reconnaissance.

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:10.990
What? We’re boarding that thing?

00:22:10.990 --> 00:22:12.490
I’m a bit…

00:22:12.490 --> 00:22:16.460
Don’t be unreasonable. You should
just be thankful Chor Tempest…

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:19.980
She’s right.
That old boat should do just fine.

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:23.480
I don’t mind at all!

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:47.920
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:52.160
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:59.190
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:06.790
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.610 --> 00:23:19.680
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.680 --> 00:23:24.890
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.890 --> 00:23:28.860
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:32.830
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:38.770
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.770 --> 00:23:44.310
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.310 --> 00:23:47.750
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.750 --> 00:23:53.420
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.420 --> 00:23:59.580
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:06.590
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:05.990 --> 00:24:07.640
Chor Tempest…

00:24:07.640 --> 00:24:12.220
…boards the antiquated ship Messis
and is on its way to the border.

00:24:14.300 --> 00:24:16.180
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:19.970
<b>Birds in a Cage</b>

00:24:17.140 --> 00:24:18.680
Birds in a Cage.
